It was also the title of a movie the last year, but really it's just symbolic and it's just

01:21.640 --> 01:25.760
meant to stand in for web developer techniques in general and not specifically Django, but

01:25.760 --> 01:28.080
I'm using it because I love it, okay?

01:28.080 --> 01:29.080
Django.

01:29.080 --> 01:30.280
All right.

01:30.280 --> 01:34.000
Number one, your laptop should be disposable, all right?

01:34.000 --> 01:36.000
Your laptop should be disposable.

01:36.000 --> 01:37.000
Never again.

01:37.000 --> 01:39.640
Never again should your laptop crash and you lose everything.

01:39.640 --> 01:40.920
Should your project be fucked?

01:40.920 --> 01:42.520
Should you be up shit quick?

01:42.520 --> 01:43.520
Should not happen.

01:43.520 --> 01:46.640
The worst thing you should do, use version control.

01:46.640 --> 01:47.640
Get on GitHub.

01:47.640 --> 01:48.640
Put your code.

01:48.640 --> 01:50.000
It doesn't have to be on the web.

01:50.000 --> 01:54.360
It can be on a server in your newsroom, but put it someplace else and start sharing it

01:54.360 --> 01:55.360
this way.

01:55.360 --> 01:56.360
All right.

01:56.360 --> 01:57.360
Two, database backups.

01:57.360 --> 02:02.680
Please, just write that ten-line conscript to back up that database every night.

